    "codeql_raw_query": "/**\n * @name Path traversal in file operations\n * @description File operations with unsanitized user input can lead to path traversal attacks\n * @kind path-problem\n * @problem.severity error\n * @id py/path-traversal-pytz\n * @tags security\n *        external/cwe/cwe-022\n */\n\nimport python\nimport semmle.python.dataflow.new.DataFlow\nimport semmle.python.dataflow.new.TaintTracking\nimport semmle.python.Concepts\nimport semmle.python.ApiGraphs\n\nmodule PathTraversalConfig implements DataFlow::ConfigSig {\n  predicate isSource(DataFlow::Node source) {\n    // Parameters to functions that might receive user input\n    source instanceof DataFlow::ParameterNode or\n    // Function arguments\n    exists(DataFlow::CallCfgNode call |\n      source = call.getArg(_)\n    )\n  }\n\n  predicate isSink(DataFlow::Node sink) {\n    // File system access operations\n    sink = any(FileSystemAccess fa).getAPathArgument()\n  }\n  \n  predicate isBarrier(DataFlow::Node node) {\n    // Path sanitization or validation\n    exists(DataFlow::CallCfgNode call |\n      call = API::moduleImport(\"os\").getMember(\"path\").getMember([\"abspath\", \"realpath\", \"normpath\"]).getACall() and\n      node = call\n    )\n  }\n}\n\nmodule PathTraversalFlow = TaintTracking::Global<PathTraversalConfig>;\nimport PathTraversalFlow::PathGraph\n\nfrom PathTraversalFlow::PathNode source, PathTraversalFlow::PathNode sink\nwhere PathTraversalFlow::flowPath(source, sink)\nselect sink.getNode(), source, sink, \"Potential path traversal from $@.\", source.getNode(), \"user-controlled input\"",
    "hypothesis": "Check for path traversal vulnerabilities in file operations, particularly when loading timezone data files. The package uses os module and likely reads timezone data from the filesystem.",
